From 3bdeda7968ab1fa1731b31a441d280701c4b3f40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:44:28 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Remix, a site as a mobile-app prototype from its
 own data (behind a flag, off)

Remix (localStorage meridian.remix = '1'; off by default) adds "Remix as a
mobile app" to the Boost editor on a site that has a Remix: so far only
dodopizza.ru. It saves a boost named "Remix: mobile app" whose script
(meridian/remix.ts, generated from the spike's remix.js) runs in the Boosts'
isolated world and draws the site's live menu as an app in a phone frame:
feed, category tabs, product sheet with sizes, a cart kept in the page. The
script only sends GETs to the site's own menu endpoint and never orders.
The tab reloads to show it; "Undo Remix" deletes the boost and reloads, and
the site is back as it was. Off, nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
